  "description": "<p>Batch ingests of large \"archival\" base-64 encoded objects were failing with a StorageDeviceException error. The following was also appearing in fedora.log: com.mysql.jdbc.MysqlDataTruncation: Data truncation: Data too long for column 'dcRelation' at row 1</p>\n\n<p>In the table doFields, the column type for dcRelation was altered from TEXT to LONGTEXT and ingests were successful. Could Fedora automatically create the table with this column type?</p>",
